I was wondering this recently, so I took a look at the code.  The timeout
is a random number, with an average of about 300, but a broad distribution.
I'm too lazy to work out just what that distribution is, but I'd say that
600 is pretty safe.  I usually wait about 1000 myself.  If you are the
Hand of Elbereth (or steal souls for Arioch) it adds an extra 1000 or so,
and another 1000 if you have "killed" the Wizard.

If you have a major problem, you are allowed to pray 200 turns before the
timeout, and if you have a minor complaint, 100 turns before.

Sacrificing takes time off the timeout.  When you sacrifice, if you get
an object, or a clover, or no message after the part about the flame, then
your timeout has gone to zero and it's safe to pray.

